# LC05: Application definitions — draft CRUD, revision pinning, release-candidate/release lifecycle.
# IDs, versions and revisions always come from actual responses (REPLACE_FROM_* placeholders).
@baseUrl = http://localhost:51870
@tenant = Testmandant
@appId = REPLACE_FROM_CREATE_RESPONSE
@revisionId = REPLACE_FROM_REVISION_RESPONSE
@candidateId = REPLACE_FROM_RELEASE_CANDIDATE_RESPONSE

### Create draft revision 1 (use configured HTTP-client authentication)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/applications
Content-Type: application/json

{"tenantId":"{{tenant}}","key":"lc05-app","name":"LC05 application","expectedVersion":0,"content":"{\"pages\":[{\"id\":\"home\",\"route\":\"/home\"}]}"}

### Read the draft (current mutable revision)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/applications/{{appId}}?tenantId={{tenant}}

### Read fixed revision 1 (must not change on later updates)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/applications/{{appId}}/revisions/1?tenantId={{tenant}}

### Update draft with expectedVersion=1 -> becomes revision 2 (stale expectedVersion yields 409, no data loss)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/applications/{{appId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"tenantId":"{{tenant}}","key":"lc05-app","name":"LC05 application v2","expectedVersion":1,"content":"{\"pages\":[{\"id\":\"home\",\"route\":\"/home\"},{\"id\":\"settings\",\"route\":\"/settings\"}]}"}

### Negative: concurrent update with stale expectedVersion must be rejected (409)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/applications/{{appId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"tenantId":"{{tenant}}","key":"lc05-app","name":"Stale write","expectedVersion":1,"content":"{\"pages\":[{\"id\":\"home\",\"route\":\"/home\"}]}"}

### Read fixed revision 1 again (unchanged despite the update above)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/applications/{{appId}}/revisions/1?tenantId={{tenant}}

### Create release candidate from explicitly pinned revision 2
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/applications/{{appId}}/revisions/2/release-candidate?tenantId={{tenant}}

### Get the release candidate
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/applications/release-candidates/{{candidateId}}?tenantId={{tenant}}

### Release the candidate (204)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/applications/release-candidates/{{candidateId}}/release?tenantId={{tenant}}

### Negative: drafting a new revision after release must not displace the released one
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/applications/{{appId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"tenantId":"{{tenant}}","key":"lc05-app","name":"LC05 application v3","expectedVersion":2,"content":"{\"pages\":[{\"id\":\"home\",\"route\":\"/home\"},{\"id\":\"admin\",\"route\":\"/admin\"}]}"}

### Released read: returns the pinned revision 2 only (never the v3 draft) — no draft leak
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/applications/{{appId}}/released-revision?tenantId={{tenant}}

### Negative: read the release candidate / released revision from another tenant (403)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/applications/{{appId}}/released-revision?tenantId=Testmandant-fremd
